// Ghidra 12.2 reports a bit-field read as ZPULL (unsigned) or SPULL (signed)
// and a bit-field write as INSERT.  The operands are the container, then for
// INSERT the new field value, then the bit position and the bit count.  The
// containers here are 4, 8 and 1 bytes wide.
//
// No operation may be dropped.
// LOG-NOT: unsupported mnemonic
// LOG-NOT: op-dropped
// LOG-NOT: return-synthesized
